<title>KUWAIT: Kuwaiti signs deal for $669 mln Egypt project - KUNA.</title>
<headline>Kuwaiti signs deal for $669 mln Egypt project - KUNA.</headline>
<dateline>KUWAIT 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Kuwaiti businessman has signed a contract to build a huge tourist project in Egypt worth some 200 million dinars ($669 million), Kuwait's official news agency KUNA said.</p>
<p>&quot;A Kuwaiti businessman signed a contract here tonight with the Egyptian government to erect a sea-side tourist city (resort) in Egypt at a total value of about...200 million dinars,&quot; KUNA said in a despatch from Cairo on Tuesday night.</p>
<p>The three-stage, 15-year project, by Khaled Yousef al-Marzouq, involves building three five-star hotels, a golf club, a yacht club, residential areas and trade centres in Egypt's Sinai Peninsula, the agency added.</p>
<p>It gave no details on project financing.</p>
<p>($1=0.299 dinar)</p>
</text>
